.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH dfdu-clean 1  "dfdu-clean " 
.SH NAME
dfdu\-clean \- Delete what `report` recommends (dry run unless \-\-yes)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdfdu clean\fR [\fB\-\-min\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-category\fR] [\fB\-\-older\-than\fR] [\fB\-\-safety\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-allow\-commands\fR] [\fB\-\-finish\-staged\fR] [\fB\-\-restore\-staged\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-x\fR|\fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR] [\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR] [\fB\-\-network\fR] [\fB\-\-mft\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Delete what `report` recommends (dry run unless \-\-yes)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-size\fR \fI<SIZE>\fR
Only matches at least this big (`100M`, `1.5GiB`, `500 KB`)
.TP
\fB\-\-category\fR \fI<CATEGORY>\fR
Only these categories (comma separated): an id such as `dev.build`, or its first part (`dev`) for all of them
.TP
\fB\-\-older\-than\fR \fI<AGE>\fR
Only matches unchanged for this long (`30d`, `2w`, `12h`; a bare number is days)
.TP
\fB\-\-safety\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR [default: regenerable]
Matches this safe or safer are considered: safe, regenerable or review. Manual and protected matches are never deleted
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Every match that passes the filters, not only the recommended ones (recommended: `safe` above the rule\*(Aqs minimum size, `regenerable` also unchanged for the rule\*(Aqs minimum age, nothing changed in the last 7 days)
.TP
\fB\-\-mode\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: trash]
trash (the default; frees no space until the trash is emptied), stage (moved aside at once, then deleted; what is left after a crash is offered by `dfdu recover`) or delete (permanently)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
trash
.IP \(bu 2
stage
.IP \(bu 2
delete
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Delete. Without it nothing is changed: the plan is printed
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-commands\fR
Run the owning tool\*(Aqs cleanup command for matches cleaned up that way (`docker system prune`, `go clean \-cache`). Without it they are skipped
.TP
\fB\-\-finish\-staged\fR
First delete what earlier sessions left staged (`dfdu recover` lists it)
.TP
\fB\-\-restore\-staged\fR
First put back what earlier sessions left staged
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: table]
Output: table or json (schema/clean.v1.json)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<THREADS>\fR
Worker threads
.TP
\fB\-x\fR, \fB\-\-one\-file\-system\fR
Stay on the filesystem of the scanned directory (the default; overrides \-\-cross\-mounts and \-\-network given before it)
.TP
\fB\-\-cross\-mounts\fR
Descend into other local filesystems (disks, tmpfs)
.TP
\fB\-\-network\fR
Descend into network filesystems (NFS, SMB, sshfs and other FUSE network mounts); with or without \-\-cross\-mounts
.TP
\fB\-\-mft\fR
Windows, as administrator: read each NTFS volume\*(Aqs master file table instead of listing its directories, which is much faster on large volumes. Volumes whose table cannot be read are listed as usual
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

